this chat) | Repos, issues, PRs |
| Official X/Twitter API | **No connector installed** | Cannot assume search, historical posts, or following-list APIs work here |
| Browser (box) | **Yes** (manual/GUI workflows) | Not a substitute for reliable X API at scale |
| On-chain RPC | **Not yet provisioned** | Need Alchemy (or similar) API key + archive for indexing |
| Signing / custody | **Must never live in the LLM** | Separate signer service / hardware / MPC |

**X/Twitter reality (2026):** Official self-serve X API is pay-per-use / credit-based. Recent search is typically limited (often ~7 days on self-serve). Full-archive search is generally **Enterprise / sales-led** or third-party. Following/followers reads are billable per resource. Continuous monitoring of many accounts + keyword firehose is a **budget and product decision**, not a free built-in.

---

## 2. Architecture (strict separation of concerns)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         CONTROL PLANE                            │
│  Policy engine · Kill switch · Approval store · Audit log        │
│  (LLM cannot mutate policies or authorize trades)                │
└───────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬───────────────────┘
                │                             │
┌───────────────▼──────────────┐  ┌───────────▼───────────────────┐
│     DATA COLLECTION          │  │     RESEARCH / SCORING        │
│  Indexers · RPC/WSS · APIs   │  │  Workers + LLM as analyst     │
│  Launchpad listeners         │  │  Evidence graph + citations   │
│  Wallet watchers             │  │  Meme vs utility frameworks   │
│  Social (optional, budgeted) │  │  Outputs: OpportunityReport   │
└───────────────┬──────────────┘  └───────────┬───────────────────┘
                │                             │
                └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                               │
                ┌──────────────▼──────────────┐
                │   APPROVAL GATEWAY          │
                │   Human approves proposal   │
                │   Expiry · revalidation     │
                └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                               │
                ┌──────────────▼──────────────┐
                │   SIGNING SERVICE           │
                │   Keys NEVER in LLM host    │
                │   Policy-checked intents    │
                └──────────────┬──────────────┘
                ┌──────────────▼──────────────┐
                │   EXECUTION + MONITORING    │
                │   Simulate · submit · track │
                │   Pre-approved sell rules   │
                └─────────────────────────────┘
```

### Component rules

| Component | May use LLM? | May hold keys? | May submit txs? |
|-----------|--------------|----------------|-----------------|
| Collectors | No (or only for parsing with schemas) | No | No |
| Research/scoring | Yes (analyst) | No | No |
| Approval UI/API | No | No | No |
| Signer | No | Yes | Signs only |
| Executor | No | No | Yes, with signed payload + policy check |
| Monitoring | Limited | No | Only via pre-approved sell paths |

**Untrusted content fence:** Any text from X, websites, docs, or GitHub READMEs is data. It must never change risk limits, approval state, or signer policy.

---

## 3. Required APIs, indexers, RPC, X — limitations and cost sketch

### 3.1 Must-have (MVP on-chain)

| Service | Use | Est. cost (order of magnitude) | Notes |
|---------|-----|--------------------------------|-------|
| Alchemy Robinhood Chain RPC + WSS | Live reads, logs, sims | Free tier → paid as volume grows | Official recommended |
| Archive RPC (Alchemy / Dwellir / similar) | Historical state, backfill | Paid | Required for deployer history |
| Blockscout explorer API | Contract metadata, verification status | Usually free/rate-limited | `robinhoodchain.blockscout.com` |
| Uniswap subgraph / pool events (or self-index) | Pool creates, swaps, liquidity | Free if self-index; hosted varies | Prefer event indexing on your stack |
| Launchpad event indexing (Pons / Pools.trade factories) | New token discovery | Engineering time | **Custom**; addresses must be verified |
| PostgreSQL + object storage | Evidence, reports, blobs | Commodity cloud | Core system of record |
| Redis / queue (e.g. NATS/SQS) | Job fan-out | Commodity | Hourly research + live triggers |

### 3.2 Strongly recommended (pre-live trading)

| Service | Use | Est. cost | Notes |
|---------|-----|-----------|-------|
| Zerion / Alchemy Data API | Wallet + portfolio enrichment | Paid | Official partner |
| Allium or similar warehouse | Analytics / backtests | Paid / enterprise | Official partner listed |
| CoinGecko (or DefiLlama) | Market cap / listings | Free–paid | Cross-check; RH-specific coverage may lag |
| TRM Labs (optional) | Sanctions / risk labels | Enterprise | Official partner |
| Tenderly / local fork / `eth_call` sims | Buy/sell simulation | Free–paid | Critical before approve |

### 3.3 Social / X (phase later unless budgeted)

| Option | Capability | Cost reality | Recommendation |
|--------|------------|--------------|----------------|
| Official X API pay-per-use | Recent search, user reads, following lists | Per-resource; monitoring 400+ accounts + keywords adds up fast | Start with **narrow** watchlists (project accounts + 20–50 KOLs), not full firehose |
| Official full-archive / stream | Historical + realtime at scale | Enterprise / sales | Defer |
| Third-party social APIs | Cheaper historical/search | ToS/legal/reliability risk | Evaluate carefully; treat as untrusted |
| Manual / curated lists | Human-maintained handles | Labour | Best for MVP credibility |

**Do not design MVP to require** continuous X following-list diffs for every project. That is a Phase 2+ cost centre.

### 3.4 Trading / execution infra

| Piece | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| Dedicated low-latency RPC + optional colocated submitter | FCFS arrival competition |
| Sequencer feed (`wss://feed.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com`) | Observe ordering / confirm inclusion (validate usefulness empirically) |
| Router (Uniswap / Rialto) | Quotes + swaps |
| Simulation before send | Taxes, honeypots, revert detection |
| Separate hot wallet(s) with hard caps | Blast radius |

**~50 wallets:** Legitimate uses = isolation by strategy, paper vs live, cold vs hot, venue segregation, incident containment. **Not** for evading per-wallet limits. Complexity cost: key ceremony, nonce management